
# command-palette

## shell
- label: Cmd/Ctrl+K toggles the CommandPalette on served WebUI pages — it opens when closed and closes when already open
  id: cpk
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'Cmd/Ctrl.K toggles|toggles the palette' test/browser/command-palette.test.js
  tags: [spec, command-palette, implemented]
- label: the CommandPalette is a modal dialog with a combobox input (placeholder Type a command or search...) and a grouped listbox of results
  id: cpd
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'modal dialog with combobox' test/browser/command-palette.test.js
  tags: [spec, command-palette, implemented]
- label: an empty CommandPalette query shows grouped actions prioritized by the current page, with a context chip when a run or session is open
  id: cpe
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'empty query shows grouped|context chip' test/browser/command-palette.test.js
  tags: [spec, command-palette, implemented]
- label: typing in the CommandPalette filters the grouped list; a query that matches no commands shows a no-results state plus a Search sessions fallback
  id: cpf
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'filters the grouped list|no-results' test/browser/command-palette.test.js
  tags: [spec, command-palette, implemented]
- label: Escape and clicking the CommandPalette backdrop dismiss the overlay and restore the previously focused element
  id: cpx
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'Escape and backdrop dismiss' test/browser/command-palette.test.js
  tags: [spec, command-palette, implemented]
- label: while the CommandPalette is open, keyboard focus stays inside the dialog; Tab does not move focus to the page behind it
  id: cpt
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'focus trap' test/browser/command-palette.test.js
  tags: [spec, command-palette, implemented]
- label: Arrow keys move the highlighted CommandPalette result and Enter runs it
  id: cpa
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'Arrow keys move|Enter runs' test/browser/command-palette.test.js
  tags: [spec, command-palette, implemented]
- label: the CommandPalette uses Tracequest --surface/--fg/--accent tokens and compact dark command-menu chrome (grouped rows, shortcut glyphs, no foreign widget skin)
  id: cpv
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'uses Tracequest tokens' test/browser/command-palette.test.js
  tags: [spec, command-palette, implemented]
- label: later CommandPalette result kinds register via window.TracequestPalette.registerProvider without replacing the shell
  id: cpr
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'registerProvider' test/browser/command-palette.test.js
  tags: [spec, command-palette, implemented]
- label: the CommandPalette is mounted on the Runs inventory, run/chat pages, compare, and served /view — not on standalone exported session HTML
  id: cpm
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'mounted on Runs|mounted on run|mounted on compare|mounted on served /view|not on standalone export' test/browser/command-palette.test.js
  tags: [spec, command-palette, implemented]
- label: Cmd/Ctrl+K is ignored during IME composition so CJK input does not toggle the CommandPalette mid-composition
  id: cpi
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'IME composition' test/browser/command-palette.test.js
  tags: [spec, command-palette, implemented]
- label: the shared app bar exposes a CommandPalette trigger whose label is Cmd+K on Mac and Ctrl+K elsewhere, and activating it opens the same overlay
  id: cph
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'app bar exposes a CommandPalette trigger' test/browser/command-palette.test.js
  tags: [spec, command-palette, implemented]
- label: the CommandPalette is a modal overlay object: a full-viewport dim/scrim recedes the page so the menu is the only lit surface, including the collapsed no-results state
  id: cpsr
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'full-viewport dim/scrim|modal overlay object' test/browser/command-palette.test.js
  tags: [spec, command-palette, implemented]

## search
- label: a non-empty CommandPalette query fetches GET /api/search?q= and lists the ranked session hits; an empty query does not call /api/search
  id: cpsq
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'fetches GET /api/search|empty query does not call /api/search' test/browser/command-palette-search.test.js
  tags: [spec, command-palette, palette-search, implemented]
- label: each CommandPalette session hit shows source, short session id, and prompt excerpt so the result is pickable
  id: cpidn
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'shows source, short session id, and prompt' test/browser/command-palette-search.test.js
